// spec: an explicit instantiation definition (`template struct Box<int>;`) instantiates every member of the instance, used or not ([temp.explicit] 10): a member whose body is no valid code for it is an error, as clang says ("cannot initialize a variable of type 'int' with an lvalue of type 'const char[5]'") (a guard for thread A's lazy instance members, D's review of 2026-11-08)
// pending: kpp's explicit instantiation builds the instance's static data members only, and an unused member function's errors are shown only when it is emitted, so the program builds (found by D reviewing A's lazy instance members, 2026-11-08); D
// error: explicit_instantiation_instantiates_every_member_is_error.kpp:11: error: a pointer (const char*) does not convert to int32 without a cast
template<typename T>
struct Box
{
  T value{};
  int get() const { return 1; }
  int bad() const
  {
    T x = "text";
    return 2;
  }
};
template struct Box<int>;
int main()
{
  Box<int> b;
  return b.get();
}
